context:
Spike result (2026-10-22): GO-WITH-CHANGES. Setup: the pinned omp linux-x64 18.12.1 ran in an Apple container (linux/amd64, Rosetta); the gateway ran on the owner's Mac in front of the existing broker; the reviewer env held only HOME, PATH and OMP_GATEWAY_TOKEN.

REAL results:
- scope: 401, 404 Unknown model, 403 on /v1/usage;
- all five role aliases answered;
- 6 of 7 fallback models answered (google-antigravity/gemini-4-argon is out of quota upstream);
- a real usage-limit 429 walked the chain through the gateway;
- an end-to-end runner.review at @smol on PR 3270 produced a valid verdict;
- fetch was refused with 0 canary hits; .omp/AGENTS.md was not injected.

SYNTHETIC results:
- role-keyed fallbackChains make every --model @role walk the default chain on 18.12.1, contrary to the omp docs;
- model-keyed chains restore the per-role chains.

Owner decisions (2026-10-22):
- staged cutover: owner setup first, the PR merges after, a revert is the rollback until the old secrets are deleted;
- retry.fallbackOn: usage-limit;
- fallbackChains keyed by primary model id;
- residual risk accepted: the model can read its own scoped, tailnet-only client token, and probably runner variables from its parent environ (inferred);
- one rotation after cutover.

Not tested locally: tailscale serve HTTPS, the real Actions runner, the gateway's 255 s Bun idle timeout during long thinking, Anthropic's own usage-limit classification. The first hosted runs after merge are the canary.

The cutover PR is prepared in BenchBox.wt-oracle-gateway-cutover (branch fix/oracle-gateway-cutover). Owner-only steps: launchd gateway, tailscale serve, ACL entry for the gateway port, ORACLE_GATEWAY_TOKEN and ORACLE_GATEWAY_URL secrets. After the canary: delete the old reviewer secrets and the broker ACL entry, then rotate.
